  "rationale": "The added columns provide several genuinely useful axes for explaining regional siting -- especially talent dependency, physical infrastructure, technology focus, and industry sector, which are classic drivers of agglomeration. Market_orientation is comparatively weak/generic. Groundedness is generally solid where the text is descriptive, and silent-row handling ('not_present', 'none_digital_only', 'none_unregulated') is correct. The main weakness is over-confident inference on columns like company_stage and talent_ecosystem_dependency, where labels (e.g. Accel->software_engineering, Addepar->growth_stage) are asserted beyond what the source text supports."
